  "caption": "Quinn bought barefoot shoes and ran 10km in them the very next day. The calves were not impressed.\n\nMinimal shoes don't remove load, they shift it from the knee towards the calf, Achilles and foot. Walking in them can build foot strength, but jumping in too fast is when niggles often show up.\n\nThings that often help: walk in them for a few weeks before running, add calf raises and toe and arch work, start with 5–10 minutes of running and build over two to three months, and ease off if pain becomes pinpoint or lingers.\n\nIf you have Achilles or heel pain, a past stress fracture, diabetes or reduced foot sensation, get individual advice before switching.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
